---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO, REPO_PUBLIC } from '../site';

const releases = [
  {
    version: '0.1.7',
    date: '2026-11-14',
    href: `${REPO}/releases/tag/v0.1.7`,
    items: [
      'Sessions on this Mac sit in a This Mac group in the sidebar that collapses, drags and has a group menu like any other, and new local sessions no longer land in a remote host’s group.',
      'Show sessions side by side: right-click a session in the sidebar for Open in Split, or drag it onto a pane to split that pane. Build layouts of three, four or more panes, and drag the dividers to resize them.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.1.6',
    date: '2026-11-09',
    href: `${REPO}/releases/tag/v0.1.6`,
    items: [
      'Logging out of a Linux server without lingering no longer loses sessions or brings back copies of them, and the daemon puts back a socket that was deleted under it.',
      'A session can no longer lock up: not on output that crashed its screen model, not on heavy typing while its output isn’t read, and a stuck session no longer holds up the others.',
      'Settings → Hosts has a switch for lingering, which keeps a Linux server’s sessions running after you log out.',
      'Tighter security: session sockets and files are checked to be private and yours, session settings stay off the command line, host names are checked before they reach ssh, and very long titles are cut.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.1.5',
    date: '2026-11-06',
    href: `${REPO}/releases/tag/v0.1.5`,
    items: [
      'Connecting to a server goes straight to its sessions, or opens a new session if it has none. Clicking a server in the session picker does the same.',
      'When a server refuses your SSH login, Swarm says why and offers the fix: Open in Terminal sets your key up in a new tab, where you type the server’s password into ssh itself.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.1.4',
    date: '2026-11-06',
    href: `${REPO}/releases/tag/v0.1.4`,
    items: [
      'swarmctl and swarmd work through a symlink when no daemon is running yet, as in the docs’ ln -s setup. Before, they looked for their sibling programs next to the link and failed.',
      'A daemon built from the same source now always has the same build ID, wherever it was built.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.1.3',
    date: '2026-11-04',
    href: `${REPO}/releases/tag/v0.1.3`,
    items: [
      'Remote hosts get the current swarmd again: 0.1.1 and 0.1.2 carried the 0.1.0 Linux daemon, so they left Linux hosts on it. Updating Swarm now updates them when it next connects.',
      'Linux builds of swarmd (x86_64 and aarch64) can be downloaded to set up a server by hand. See Install on a server yourself in the docs.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.1.2',
    date: '2026-11-02',
    href: `${REPO}/releases/tag/v0.1.2`,
    items: [
      'Notarized by Apple: the download opens without the security warning.',
      'Updates install themselves: Swarm checks for new versions and offers Install and Restart. Each update must carry Swarm’s release signature; your sessions keep running.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.1.1',
    date: '2026-11-02',
    href: `${REPO}/releases/tag/v0.1.1`,
    items: [
      'New app icon: the Hive. The 0.1.0 download still had the old one.',
      'A color you give a session now shows in the sidebar too, not just on its tab.',
      'swarm:// links open launch configurations in Swarm.',
      'Check for Updates… reads new releases from swarm-term.com, so it works while the repository is private.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.1.0',
    date: '2026-11-01',
    href: `${REPO}/releases/tag/v0.1.0`,
    items: [
      'Persistent sessions: tabs keep running when you close the window, quit the app or restart the daemon, and reopen with their output and blocks.',
      'Remote hosts over your own ssh setup, Linux or macOS. Swarm installs its daemon there and reconnects after sleep and network drops.',
      'The app: a session sidebar, one panel per session, split panes, a Swarm theme and system fonts, built on Warp’s open-source engine.',
      'In-place updates: running sessions move to a new version of their session process without restarting.',
      'Scrollback: 16 MB per session in memory, with optional encrypted spill to disk (swarmd spill on).',
      'swarmctl: ls, new, attach, rename, info, dump, kill and rm, locally or with --host.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base title="Swarm changelog: what's new in each release" description="Release notes for Swarm, the macOS terminal with persistent sessions: new features, fixes and updates in each version.">
  <div class="frame page">
    <p class="label"># changelog</p>
    <h1>What's new</h1>
    {releases.map((r) => (
      <section class="release">
        <div class="meta">
          {REPO_PUBLIC ? <a class="version" href={r.href}>v{r.version}</a> : <span class="version">v{r.version}</span>}
          <time datetime={r.date}>{r.date}</time>
        </div>
        <ul>
          {r.items.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .release {
    margin-top: 32px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 32px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 32px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 699px) {
    .release {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 12px;
    }
  }

  .meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    align-content: start;
  }

  .version {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  time {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }
</style>
